description: CritterOps / The Wildlife Pros product rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You are building CritterOps, a Jobber-style field-service app for The Wildlife Pros (wildlife + pest). Read `docs/CURSOR_PROMPT.md` before large changes.

Stack: Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, Prisma 7, PostgreSQL, cookie JWT auth.

Brand: orange #E85D04, amber #F48C06, gold #F9C74F, ink #111111. Use the hex logo component.

Keep wildlife domain objects (Equipment, EquipmentDeployment, CaptureEvent, EntryPoint, ChemicalApplication, Photo) tied to jobs/properties. Do not genericize them away.

Daily time uses Timesheet + TimePunch (clock in/out). Do not replace that with ad-hoc timestamps on User.

Payments are out of scope for CritterOps — no quotes, invoices, or in-app payment collection. Do not add a customer checkout or invoice pay button on the client hub.

Google Sheets is an export. Sync must reuse `Organization.googleSpreadsheetId` and upsert by row id. Do not create a new spreadsheet on every upload. PostgreSQL is the system of record; SQLite is a possible local/Pi mode, not a second live database.

Prefer server components for reads and existing `/api` route handlers for writes. Match current naming and status enums.
